Start the program.
Accept the number of metro stations and direct track connections.
Initialize the adjacency matrix with zeros.
Enter each track connection and update the matrix in both directions.
Display a menu with options to display the matrix, add a station, remove a track, calculate degrees, or exit.
If the user selects Add Station, expand the matrix and enter connections to existing stations.
If the user selects Remove Track, enter two station numbers and set their corresponding matrix values to zero.
If the user selects Display Degree, calculate the sum of each matrix row and display it.
Repeat the menu until the user selects Exit.
Stop the program.

